# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch O (DeepSeek)."""
DESC_O = {
    'RT:DSC2': {
        2: "Dr. Kenzo Kabuto secretly designed and developed this super robot based on Mazinger Z. Like Mazinger Z, it appears from a whirlpool upon the call of 'Mazin Go!', and is completed when Tetsuya's Brain Condor combines with its head (Fire On). Its power source is the same Photon Power Energy as Mazinger Z, but its armor is made of Super Alloy New Z, which surpasses Super Alloy Z, making it even more durable than Mazinger Z. Due to its development history, many of its weapons were evolved and strengthened from Mazinger Z's arsenal. Its unique attack methods include the giant sword 'Mazinger Blade' stored in both legs, and 'Thunder Break', which stores lightning as energy and then unleashes it. Additionally, a flight device called the Scramble Dash is built into its back, allowing flight at Mach 4. Later, the 'Great Booster', which combines to improve flight performance, was completed. It was also a powerful weapon that, when rammed into enemies, exhibited destructive power equivalent to a hydrogen bomb. After the war against the Mycenae Empire ended, it was stored in the Robot Science Museum alongside Venus A and Boss Borot. In the theatrical version, there was a scene where it was seized by enemies there and fought against Grendizer.",
        12: "A saucer beast that appeared in Episode 4, 'Young Blood Burns Crimson', sent to locate Grendizer's base. It indiscriminately destroyed the city with spikes that shot out from its saucer section, and fire and missiles breathed from its mouth. It was also equipped with an electromagnetic net, easily shooting down TFOs. However, it was toyed with by the combination of Grendizer and TFO, which rushed in, and was scattered by a finishing Space Thunder.",
        13: "The strongest and final Vega Beast, which appeared from Episode 73, 'For This Beautiful Earth', and was piloted personally by Lady Gandal. It tormented Grendizer with weapons such as a beam from a protrusion on its chest that robbed enemies of sight, and high-temperature flames from its mouth. However, it was destroyed by the combination of three Spazers and the Double Harken.",
        14: "The flagship of the Vega Star Union, bearing the name of Emperor Vega. Like the TFO, its design is thought to be based on the cigar-shaped flying saucers famous at the time. During the total attack on Earth, Emperor Vega himself took command and sortied. However, it was defeated by Grendizer and Cosmo Special, the fourth Earth-made Spazer, and was scattered along with Emperor Vega's ambitions.",
        20: "A Mecha Yosaiki piloted by Ikkakuki that appeared from Episode 1, 'Getter Robo Revives!'. Besides the giant pincer on one arm, its weapons were varied, including beams from its eyes and shots from its horn. As a vanguard of the Hyakki Empire, it attacked Saotome Research Institute to steal the Getter Ray amplifier. Against the Getter Team, who were not yet used to the new Getter Robo, it used the cowardly tactic of taking Genki hostage. However, once the hostage was recaptured, it was easily defeated by a Getter Beam.",
        21: "Appearing in episode 2, 'The Terror of the Hyakki Empire's Mystery', this is a Hyakki Machine piloted by Dokuganki. It advanced through the ground by rotating the hook claws on both hands, and planned an attack on the Saotome Research Institute from underground. However, in underground combat, it was defeated by the Getter Liger, which had the upper hand.",
        22: "Appearing in episode 16, 'Deadly Battle! The Road of a Stormy Man', this is a Hyakki Machine developed by Tekkoki himself. Its performance, said to have studied the Getter Robo thoroughly, was powerful, and with weapons closely resembling the Getter Robo's, such as the Tomahawk, it greatly troubled the Getter Team. However, in the midst of battle, it shielded the Getter Robo to block Hydra's interference and took damage. Even so, it challenged again, but was defeated before the Getter Dragon.",
        23: "Appearing in episode 35, 'The Old Hyakki Soldier Never Dies', this is a Hyakki Machine piloted by Gyukenki. It pressed the Getter not only with veteran swordsmanship but also with techniques like the 'Hyakki Typhoon' blown from its mouth. But when its sword was broken, it realized its defeat and deliberately took the Shine Spark on its body, exploding.",
        24: "Appearing from episode 20, 'Great Attack! Mecha Yosaiki', this is an aircraft carrier-type Hyakki Machine. Its left and right wings could carry two Hyakki Machines, and its interior housed 100 bombers and 200 fighters. With its overwhelming firepower, it bombed Tokyo and destroyed the Saotome Research Institute. But its superiority ended there, and it was shattered by the newly completed Shine Spark, becoming the first Hyakki Machine to be destroyed.",
        25: "Appearing from episode 37, 'Crisis Approaches the Waters Near Japan!', this is the strongest Hyakki Machine formed by combining five units - Mecha Koukakuki, Mecha Yamuchiki, Mecha Rimmaki, Mecha Raijuki, and Mecha Juuhouki. It boasted overwhelming power, and even after combining, it could separate back into Hyakki Machines. But this proved to be its downfall, as it was picked off one by one after separating. Incidentally, it was originally meant to be a combination of six units, but Mecha Raidenki sortied alone to buy time and was destroyed by the Getter, resulting in its current form.",
        26: "The headquarters built by the Hyakki Empire using its own unique scientific technology. It has armor sturdy enough to repel Getter attacks.\nIt normally floats on the sea, but its ability to navigate underwater made it difficult to discover. Inside, Hyakki soldiers were being modified and Hyakki machines were being developed.\nUsing a gravity control device left by Dr. Glar, it was able to fly, and during the final battle it attacked Tokyo from the air. At first there seemed to be no opening to strike, but Hayato, who had been abducted, managed to punch a hole in the outer wall. There it was hit by Shine Spark and shattered along with Emperor Bry's ambitions.",
        27: "A giant robot belonging to Blue Fixer, created from the scientific prowess of Planet S-1 and Earth.\nBlue Fixer recovered the Palsaveren that drifted to the moon. It was then remodeled with all available technology so that it could combine with two Earth combat machines, becoming the only unit on the Earth side capable of subspace combat. Like Palsaveren, it can only be piloted by Marin, an expert in subspace dynamics.\nCombination begins with Marin's call of 'Baldios, charge up!' Palsaveren forms the head, torso, and arms, Baldiprize forms the right leg, and Cateranger forms the left leg to complete the unit.\nIt uses three engines for power: a deuterium fusion engine, an anti-gravity engine, and a subspace propulsion engine, and by using them appropriately it can operate anywhere. Its speed in the atmosphere is Mach 25. In space it can fly at 30% of lightspeed, and in subspace at infinite speed.\nMain weapons include the beam 'Bald Beam' fired from the crest crystal, the sword 'Pulse Saber' stored in the chest part, and 'Thunder Flash' which fires intense plasma from the chest.\nIn Episode 26, it received reinforcement modifications, and new armaments were added, including 'Pulse Saber Drinking' using two Pulse Sabers and '3D-Valdi', an attack that creates decoys.\nIncidentally, 'Space Warrior Baldios' was broadcast for only 31 of its 39 episodes, but since all information about the later episodes has been released, it is a rare anime whose full story can be known despite the interrupted broadcast. Many settings are hidden in the unaired portions, and 'Valdiroizer' is one of them. It was to be Baldios's final and strongest weapon used in the unaired Episode 38, a suicidal attack that would destroy Baldios itself if used.",
        28: "A spaceship built for the purpose of destroying the satellite Ganymede, which was transported between Earth and the Sun by the Aldebaron army. But in reality it is not a spaceship at all; it is a suicide weapon with a 0% survival rate, as the pilot is caught in Ganymede's explosion with no time to escape.\nWhen the launch booster is separated in space, its speed reaches lightspeed, so piloting it required knowledge of subspace dynamics and piloting skill equal to Marin's.\nDespite knowing there was absolutely no chance of survival, Marin volunteered as pilot. But David, assigned to Blue Fixer as a candidate for the New Palsaveren pilot, also volunteered, and in the end he was chosen.\nShowing piloting skill that made Marin say he was 'better than myself', David charged while murmuring the name of his beloved Quinnstein, and succeeded in destroying Ganymede, fulfilling his mission.",
        30: "The first Earth attack machine of the Aldebaron army, appearing in Episode 4 'The Day of Subspace Dive'.\nIt normally has an egg-like shape, but transforms into this form during combat, capturing opponents within its tentacles and damaging them with electric shocks.\nIt lured Baldiprize and Cateranger into the deep sea and tried to crush them with water pressure, but was shot down by a single thrust of the Pulse Saber of Baldios, which achieved its first combination.",
        31: "A super-reaction robot developed by Aphrodia, appearing in Episode 27 'The Spy I Believed In'.\nIts main weapons are beams fired from its eyes and chest, and an attack that launches its lower arms.\nIt had the ability to predict actions, evading all attacks and tormenting the newly powered-up Baldios. However, since it could only predict Baldios's actions, it lost its balance against the combination attacks of the three separated machines due to Marin's quick thinking, and was finished off by a subspace beam.",
        35: "The flagship of Aldebaron.\nIn the unaired episode 34, 'The Long Afternoon of Earth,' Gattler himself boarded it and commanded from the front lines.\nIt possessed formidable combat power, and no warship - not even on Earth, but also in the Aldebaron army - could rival it. Its angular appearance suggested it concealed the power to destroy even stars.\nIt was sunk by a suicide attack from the mini Palsaburn, piloted by Tsukikage, which wrapped nuclear melt in a subspace shower.",
        37: "A super robot developed by Dr. Kazami.\nKuRaiOh forms the upper body, UMinariOh the right leg, and RikuShinOh the left leg, while Big Wing covers KuRaiOh's chest and back in a combination that creates the super robot God Sigma, powered by Trinity Energy.\nBasically, the pilots of the three machines - KuRaiOh, UMinariOh, and RikuShinOh - become its pilots, but it is also possible to control it with only the KuRaiOh pilot alone. However, in that case, there is a disadvantage in that the power of UMinariOh and RikuShinOh cannot be fully utilized.\nIts armaments include the 'Finger Needle,' which fires energy shots from the fingertips; the 'God Tomahawk,' which can be thrown or held in hand; and the 'Spin Saucer,' a spiked disc thrown sidearm. Its special moves are various sword techniques using the 'MusouSw' stored in Big Wing. The variations are truly diverse, including 'Tangoguzari,' 'Gyakugesagiri,' 'Jumonjigiri,' 'Kabutowari,' 'Suiheigiri,' 'Morohazuki,' 'Morohagaeshi,' 'Morotegiri,' 'Denkougiri,' and 'Ichimonjigiri.'\nLater, to counter the Cosmo Zaurus coated with special plating, the 'Sigma Breast' ray, fired from the wing tips and capable of stripping the plating, was added.",
        39: "Cosmo Zaurus No. 1, which appeared from episode 1, 'Ike, Warrior of Io.'\nIt attacked Trinity City with various destruction rays and the ability to create whirlpools. However, it was destroyed by the combination of KuRaiOh, UMinariOh, and RikuShinOh, and an attack using the secret weapon 'Search Missile.'",
        40: "A Cosmo Zaurus that appeared in episode 19, 'Robot Cannot Launch.'\nIt had the appearance of a giant carnivorous dinosaur, and its hug attack, delivered from a body that surpassed even God Sigma, was powerful. However, it was cut in two at the torso by the MusouSw horizontal slash.",
        41: "A Cosmo Zaurus with a hedgehog's body and a bat's face that appeared in episode 38, 'Departure to Io.'\nIt invaded through the seabed to nullify Trinity Base's barrier and attacked the base from within with shock missiles and solvent missiles. In the end, it was cut into a cross by the MusouSw and scattered.",
        43: "A giant robot controlled by Gagan that appeared in the final episode 'Departure to the Future.' It was completed when the surface of Gagan's fortress collapsed and the glowing object inside transformed. Possessing a body far larger than God Sigma and armor sturdy enough to block even the Sigma Breast, it overwhelmed God Sigma by wielding an axe in its right hand and a morning star in its left, firing flames from its mouth and penetrating lasers from eight holes in its chest. It cornered God Sigma to the brink of defeat, but was struck through the neck along with its hammer by a suicidal attack using the Big Wing, and exploded, resulting in a mutual destruction with God Sigma.",
        44: "A super robot developed by the Bial people to fight against Gaizock. The Zambird, which forms the head and chest, the Zambull, which forms the arms and abdomen, and the ZamBase, which forms the waist and legs, combine into a giant robot bearing the appearance of justice and mystery with the shout 'Zambot Combination In!' The combination activates the ion engines, generating power worthy of the name 'Invincible Superman.' Its main weapons include the trident blade 'Zambot Grap' fired from the arms, the cross-shaped shuriken 'Zambot Buster' on the knees, and the 'Buster Missile' launched from its protrusions. Its ultimate attack, 'Zambot Moon Attack,' fires a crescent-shaped energy bullet from the horns on its head, and several different poses are used when performing it. In the final battle, Zambull and ZamBase were destroyed without a trace due to a suicidal charge. Such a depiction of the main mecha was the first in the history of robot anime.",
        47: "A reconnaissance Mecha Boost that appeared in episode 1 'Zambo Ace Appears.' It could dig through the ground using the blades on the tips of its tentacles, and also fired lasers from its mouth and homing missiles from its waist. Kappei's intuition saw through its weakness in the abdomen, and it was destroyed by a grenade fired from the Zambo Magnum.",
        48: "A Mecha Boost that appeared in episode 7 'Farewell! My Friend' and attacked refugees in the Yokkaichi area. It fired poisonous gas-laden flames from its mouth, electrified barbed wire from its claws, and drills and missiles from its forehead. In the first battle, it put Zambo Ace and Zambull, who could not combine due to the absence of ZamBase, in a difficult spot. When it appeared again, it faced Zambot 3 and was destroyed by a consecutive attack from Zambot Blow into Moon Attack.",
        49: "A Mecha Boost that appeared in episode 18 'Aki and Kappei' and attacked the evacuation ship carrying Aki. It tormented Zambo Ace with beams from its eyes, electric shocks from its arm tentacles, and a charge attack by rotating its lower body. However, it was destroyed by an unexpected attack from Kappei, burning with rage over Aki's death, which utilized the missiles of Zambull.",
        50: "A Mekabuust that sortied to protect Bandock, appearing in episode 21 'Decisive Battle! The God Family'.\nIt fired missiles from the huge cannon in its head, a particle laser from both shoulders with enough power to cancel out the Moon Attack, and released wires from the spiked iron ball at the tip of its tail.\nIt was destroyed by Kappei's spirited Zambot Grapple after he learned of Heizaemon and Umee's suicide attack.",
        51: "Its official name is 'Red Knight Deathcain'.\nOne of the Death Knights that appeared in episode 22 'Butcher's Last Day'.\nIt wielded a giant barbarian sword, from the tip of which it fired beams. By combining its shield with its paired Blue Knight Helldyne, it could also create swords and iron balls.\nIt was destroyed by Gengoro's self-sacrificing suicide attack, set up to protect Hanae.",
        52: "Its official name is 'Blue Knight Helldyne'.\nOne of the Death Knights that appeared in episode 22 'Butcher's Last Day'.\nIt wielded a giant lancer, from the tip of which it fired beams. By combining its shield with its paired Red Knight Deathcain, it could also create swords and iron balls.\nIt was destroyed by Gengoro's self-sacrificing suicide attack, set up to protect Hanae.",
        53: "The mobile fortress that served as Gaizock's home base.\nIt could operate anywhere - on land, in the sea, or in space - and its interior contained Butcher's command room and the Mekabuust production factory.\nIt fired Bandock Cannons from both arms, large missiles from its mouth, and destruction rays from its eyes, and also attacked with space mines and extensible legs. It could generate a powerful barrier and possessed high defensive strength. The head could be detached from the main body for independent use, as was done when Butcher himself launched an attack.\nThe head was destroyed by a direct hit from the ion cannon that Zambot 3 received from Beal I, and the main body was destroyed by an attack from within by Zambo Ace.",
        55: "A super robot completed when Banjo seized a prototype Megaborg developed on Mars by Haran Creation and modified it.\nIt possessed a transformable mechanism with three stages, allowing it to change into the heavy fighter Dai Fighter and the heavy tank Daitank. It carried the small transformable fighter Mach Attacker internally, and that cockpit block moved through the body to become the pilot's seat of Daitarn 3.\nIts main weapons included the sword with a beam blade 'Daitarn Zambar', the fan-shaped 'Daitarn Fan' that could also be used as a shield, and the 'Daitarn Web', in which the cross on the arm transformed into a shuriken. Aside from these, it also contained numerous other weapons across its body, including missiles, cannons, and snappers.\nIts ultimate technique, the 'Sun Attack', was performed with the call 'Borrowing the power of the sun, now the killing Sun Attack!' as it fired a light sphere from the sun emblem on its forehead. Other patterns of this call existed, and there were also times when it was called out but never fired.\nIncidentally, piloting it seemed to be very simple, as Garrison, Beauty, Reika, and even Toppo all operated it.",
        57: "The tank form of Daitarn 3. It transforms with the call of 'Change Daitank!' and is used in rough terrain or underground. The 'Daitarn Cannon' fired from the legs serves as its main gun.",
        64: 'A second-generation Gauwalk (bipedal) weapon of the Free Space Corps, to which Katsura and Olson belonged. It is capable of high-speed combat in flyer form as well as ground combat in Gauwalk form. Its legs serve not only as landing gear but also have thrusters at the bottom that enhance flight propulsion. Though it has no arms, manipulators are built into the lower fuselage, allowing for fine work. Katsura used these to activate an unadjusted time-space vibration bomb, which sent him and the Bronco II into the chaotic time century twenty years later. In that world, it was heavily damaged in a battle to help Gloma, and after repairs and modifications it was reborn as the Orguss.',
        73: 'An attack carrier operated by the Chiram military. It carries numerous devices, and its deck is fitted with ten silos for launching large missiles. Inside, there is also a conference room where commander-class officers gather.',
        101: 'The third ship of the three Iron Gear-type vessels built. Its armor and output are enhanced, making it the most capable of the three. Under the mental control of the Innocent, Elche served as its captain and challenged the Iron Gear carrying Jiron and the others. However, it was no match for the Iron Gear of Cattset and the others, who had greater skill in handling ships, and it was wrecked.',
        102: 'The Walker Machine form of the Gear Gear. With Elche, brainwashed by the Innocent, serving as captain, it engaged in fierce close combat with the Iron Gear carrying Jiron and the others. However, it was outmatched by the Iron Gear of Cattset and the others, who had greater skill in ship handling, and was broken apart.',
        103: "The Titans developed this mobile suit independently at Gryps I. It is a redesign of the original Gundam, but it abolishes the core block system and achieves high mobility through the adoption of a movable frame. New technologies are also incorporated throughout the machine, including a linear-seat cockpit with a panoramic monitor and a detachable vulcan pod system. After being seized from the Titans by Kamille and others, its color scheme was changed from black to white. By combining with the G-Defenser, which was developed later, it became possible to improve firepower, armor, and extend its cruising range.\n\nIt was developed by Anaheim Electronics, and became the AEUG's transformable mobile suit. It is the culmination of the know-how cultivated in the Z Project, combining the movable frame technology of the Gundam Mk-II with the idea of the Flying Armor. The adoption of Gundarium Gamma armor and a new generator achieved outstanding mobility. In addition, it became possible to use the Hyper Mega Launcher, a handheld weapon with power comparable to the Mega Bazooka Launcher. Furthermore, by transforming into the Waverider, it demonstrates tremendous range and acceleration. It is a machine capable of performing in all situations, such as atmospheric entry on its own, independent flight within the atmosphere, and combat operations carrying a wingman on its back. Later, the installation of the Bio-Sensor, a simplified psycommu, gave it the ability to follow Kamille's sharpened reactions. At the same time, however, inexplicable phenomena not included in the specifications were also confirmed, such as interfering with enemy mobile suit movements and stopping them.",
        106: "Developed by Anaheim Electronics, this is the AEUG's transformable mobile suit. It is the culmination of the know-how cultivated through the Z Project, completed by combining the movable frame technology of the Gundam Mk-II with the idea of the flying armor. The adoption of Gundarium Gamma for the armor material and a new generator achieves outstanding mobility. In addition, it became possible to use the Hyper Mega Launcher, a portable weapon with power comparable to the Mega Bazooka Launcher. Furthermore, by transforming into the Waverider, it demonstrates immense range and acceleration. It is a unit capable of operating in all situations, including atmospheric entry on its own, solo flight within the atmosphere, and carrying a wingman on its back for combat operations. Later, with the installation of the Bio-Sensor, a simplified psycommu, it gained responsiveness that tracked Kamille's honed reactions. However, at the same time, the manifestation of inexplicable phenomena not included in the specifications was also confirmed, such as interfering with the movements of enemy mobile suits to halt them.",
        134: "This is a new AEUG battleship built at Amman on the Moon. It is equipped with three mobile suit catapults at the front and one at the rear, and has a large mobile suit carrying capacity. Henken, the former captain of the first Argama, served as its captain, and it performed comparably to the Argama under Bright's command. It is said to be one of four Irish-class ships built at Amman, but no other ships of the same class appear in the theatrical version. In the final battle, it advanced to shield Emma, who was being toyed with by a Hambrabi, and was shot down and sunk by Yazan. The fact that this action, which was Henken's unilateral decision in the TV version, was changed to the consensus of the bridge in the theatrical version shows how popular Emma was with the crew in the latter.",
        138: "A large space battleship secretly developed by the Titans at Gryps. As the flagship, it is also a symbol of the Titans. It has a large mobile suit capacity and numerous catapult decks that allow them to launch in a short time. It is also excellent in anti-ship bombardment capability, being equipped with many large-caliber long-range mega particle cannons. Initially, Scirocco served as its captain and achieved results such as subduing the city of Von Braun on the Moon. Later, Jamitov, who saw Scirocco as a threat, gave the ship to Basque. It sank during the battle with Scirocco, who had taken control of the Titans, attacked by Yazan, who had defected to Scirocco's side.",
        141: "A prototype mobile suit developed by Anaheim Electronics with the aim of mass-producing the Zeta Gundam. Its name is an abbreviation for 'Refined Gundam Zeta.' The transformation mechanism was eliminated, and it achieves a cruising form by combining with the Back Weapon System that envelops the machine. However, since the system is jettisoned when transforming to mobile suit form, once separated it cannot be re-equipped on the spot, making it a machine lacking in flexibility. It achieves both high mobility and firepower, and its performance as a mobile suit is itself very high. However, due to its high production cost, mass production was shelved. The one completed unit was assigned to the Londo Bell unit pursuing Neo Zeon. Amuro used it in the early stages, and Kayra took over in the middle stages. In the final stages, Chan boarded it to deliver the Psycho Frame to Amuro. However, it was shot down by a beam fired by Hathaway, who had flown into a rage at Quess's death.",
        142: "Anaheim Electronics developed this Newtype-only mobile suit in response to a request from the Londe Bell. The pilot, Amuro, was personally in charge of its design. Because it was developed by analyzing the performance of past Gundams and incorporating the latest technology, it was completed as an ultra-high-performance machine that seemed anything but hastily built. The Psycho Frame built into the cockpit area achieves exceptional mobility and response. It is also the first Gundam-type mobile suit to use the psycommu weapon Fin Funnel. These are larger than normal funnels and correspondingly more powerful. Besides use as a weapon, several units can be linked together to generate an I Field and form an anti-beam barrier, making it useful for both offense and defense. In order to stop Neo Zeon's Axis drop, he challenged Char's Sazabi, which also had a Psycho Frame, to a decisive battle and won. Afterwards, he struggled to push Axis back. His figure inspired other machines, regardless of ally or enemy, to follow, and the hearts of all who witnessed it became one. At that time, a shining force field was formed by the Psycho Frame, and its influence altered the trajectory of Axis.",
        146: "A mobile suit excavated from a Mountain Cycle in the territory of Rujana. It bore the name of the territory's lord, Lord Borjarnon, and was deployed to the Suicide Squad of the Rujana Militia. Its appearance closely resembled the Principality of Zeon's MS-06 Zaku II (indeed, the Red Team called it a Zaku), but judging by the shape of its cockpit and its performance, it was believed to be a replica. It had excellent versatility, such as being usable in space with minor modifications, and it excelled at group combat using the diverse armaments excavated along with the unit. A type closely resembling the MS-05 Zaku I was also excavated, and in the Suicide Squad, Captain Gavane used it as his personal machine. However, after it was destroyed in battle, Gavane switched to a standard unit.",
        152: 'A melee-combat-focused mobile suit that Corin personally modified from a mobile suit excavated from a Mountain Cycle on the Moon. Its main armament is the Minchi Drill, which Corin also modified from a civilian excavation heavy machine. It can use the spine structure running from its head to its tail to transform into a high-speed walking form reminiscent of a dinosaur. In transformed mode, it can deliver a headbutt using its head as a bludgeoning weapon.',
        166: "A mobile suit that the Space Revolutionary Army used as a mainstay during the 7th Space War. The one Ennil uses is an improved model, purchased from the Sea Vulture trader Rumark and painted in her personal color, blue. Its propulsion and other aspects are considerably enhanced compared to a standard Jenice, and thanks to Ennil's skill, it could hold its own even against the new-model Variant. In the final battle, it was refitted for space specifications and went into space alongside the Freeden II, but because it could not keep up with the speed of the high-performance machines such as the Gundams, it was assigned to directly escort the Freeden II. That was a modest yet important role: protecting the place for everyone to return to.",
        167: "A mobile armor that Rumark, a Sea Vulture trader with whom Ennil was close, built from salvaged parts. Its mobility was impeccable - when Ennil happened to witness the Gundam Double X and was pursued by the New Federation Forces, she outran the new-model mobile suit Varient. However, due to insufficient firepower, it could not match the Gundams; it was captured by the Gundam Ashtaron and shot down by the Gundam Virsago. The unit's name means 'hope' in the language of Rumark's homeland. For Ennil, who began traveling with the Freeden after it was shot down by the Frost Brothers, this was truly the machine that brought her hope.",
        170: "The Rashvent is a prototype mobile suit developed by the New Federation Forces. Like the Gundam types, it is equipped with the Flash System, allowing a Newtype pilot to remotely control five bit mobile suits. Unlike those of the Gundam types, the Rashvent's bit mobile suits share the exact same appearance as the main unit, enabling combat without giving the enemy a clear target. Abel, whose Newtype abilities blossomed during battle, piloted the unit and fought on par with or better than Garrod, Jamil, and Witz simultaneously. However, the battle was decided when Garrod, acting on Tiffa's advice, saw through the decoy and landed a decisive blow on the real unit.",
        171: "The Gadeel is a high-mobility mobile armor developed by the New Federation Forces. Its form - a fighter jet silhouette with a cockpit resembling a mobile suit's head and a beam rifle gripped by manipulators - stands out considerably compared to other mobile suits and mobile armors. It was designed to secure air supremacy, and in an aerial battle against the Gundam Airmaster, it heavily damaged its opponent. However, it was shot down in an instant by the improved Gundam Airmaster Burst.",
        178: "The Impulse Gundam, a unit of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series,' is shown here in its Force Silhouette configuration. The Impulse Gundam is characterized by the 'Deuterion Beam Power Transmission System,' which allows remote energy supply from the mother ship, the 'Core Splendor System,' in which the cockpit transforms into a small fighter, and the 'Silhouette System,' which allows three types of weapon units to be used according to the battle situation. Among the Impulse Gundam's three forms, this one boasts superior mobility and can fly independently even within the atmosphere, making it the most frequently used. After Shinn transferred to the Destiny Gundam, Lunamaria, who had lost her own machine, took over this unit.",
        179: "The Impulse Gundam, a unit of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series,' is shown here in its Sword Silhouette configuration. It is specialized for close combat, and its greatest weapon, the massive anti-ship sword Excalibur, can be used as twin swords when separated, or the hilts can be connected to wield it like a naginata. It can also use ranged weapons such as beam rifles as needed. Among the three Silhouettes, this one was not used as frequently. However, the Impulse Gundam's first sortie, and the time Shinn, having awakened to SEED for the first time, cornered the Earth Alliance fleet, both occurred in this configuration, making it a memorable unit.",
        180: "The Impulse Gundam, a unit of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series,' is shown here in its Blast Silhouette configuration. It is equipped with numerous weapons focused on long-range attack, including the 'Kerberos High-Energy Long-Range Beam Cannon.' Its overwhelmingly powerful firepower proves its true worth not so much in anti-mobile suit combat as in attacks against battleships and bases. Although it appeared infrequently, it performed at critical moments, such as shooting down the Abyss Gundam and preventing the firing of Requiem.",
        184: "The Blaze Zaku Phantom is a state of the Zaku Phantom, a new-generation mass-production mobile suit from ZAFT's 'New Millennium Series,' equipped with the high-mobility Blaze Wizard unit. The Zaku Phantom was mainly a commander-use mobile suit, and unlike standard units, it also mounted a shield on its right shoulder and featured a blade antenna on its head for enhanced communication and command capabilities. The Blaze Wizard is equipment that increases mobility through thrusters placed in various locations and boosts firepower through its built-in missile pods. In the series, it was used by Athrun to support the debris removal operations at Junius Seven. Despite being a mass-production type, it fought on equal or better terms against stolen Gundams.",
        188: "This is a GOUF Ignited custom unit for Heine Westenfluss. Like the Zaku Heine had been piloting until just before, it has been repainted in his personal color of orange. In the battle at the Dardanelles Strait, combined with Heine's skill, it shot down numerous Murasames. It also consistently overwhelmed the Gaia Gundam, but after its right arm was severed by the Freedom Gundam, it lost its combat capability and was bisected from behind by the Gaia Gundam's beam blade.",
        190: "This is the GuAIZ R, an improved version of the GuAIZ, ZAFT's main mobile suit from the previous war. Although its appearance has no major changes, it is equipped with a rail gun on its waist, and its shield, thrusters, and backpack have all been improved. As a result, its overall performance has been enhanced. The 'R' stands for 'Reinforce.' Its base performance is not low, but because no pilot above the level of an ordinary soldier ever boarded it, it saw no particularly notable achievements. Even when Sean and Dale, pilots belonging to the Minerva, sortied in them, they were quickly shot down by the Chaos Gundam.",
        191: 'This is a Jin High Maneuver Type 2, a specially modified version of the high-mobility type of the Jin, a mass-production mobile suit developed by ZAFT during the previous war. It was used by terrorists attempting to drop Junius Seven to Earth, to obstruct the debris removal work. Thanks to the veteran pilot, its movements rivaled even the latest models despite being an old machine. Dearka, who witnessed it, was toyed with and impressed. However, through the coordination of Yzak and the others, who were even more skilled, their numbers were gradually reduced, and the last unit was slammed into Junius Seven and shattered.',
        195: "The Windam is the successor to the Dagger L and the Earth Alliance's main mass-production mobile suit. It is highly mobile due to the large thrusters mounted on its shoulders, back, and legs. Since the Strike Pack system from the Dagger L can be used with it, this facilitated a smooth generational transition. In addition to the Jet Striker Pack, which allows flight under gravity, a Multi Striker Pack equipped with nuclear missiles also exists. Its base specs are high, but perhaps because it is often shown being shot down by the Minerva's mobile suit team, which surpasses it, no scenes of it in action were seen.",
        196: "This is Neo Roanoke's personal Windam unit. Unlike the standard units, it is painted in a purple color scheme.\nThe basic performance of the unit is no different from the standard models, but the Jet Striker pack is a special specification with the limiters removed, greatly increasing its thrust.\nBecause it was not equipped with weapons that could make use of Neo's true specialty, his spatial awareness ability, it did not have any flashy achievements, but even so it fought on par with or better than Shinn and Athrun.\nIn the battle at Berlin, it was shot down by Kira, who pierced the flight unit along with both arms. At the time it was flying at a considerable altitude, but the impact of the crash did not cause the machine to explode, so its impact resistance appears to be quite high.",
        197: "A mobile suit developed as part of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series.'\nIt is one of three new Gundams stolen from the military plant Armory One by the Earth Alliance special forces unit Phantom Pain. Due to that history, it carries model numbers from both ZAFT (ZGMF-X24S) and the Alliance (RGX-01).\nThe large thrusters on its back and waist make it a machine specialized for space combat, and within the atmosphere it can use that output for independent flight. After transforming into mobile armor form, its maneuverability improves even further.\nIts distinctive armament includes mobile weapon pods that improve on the DRAGOON system, enabling all-range attacks. Using these, it instantly destroyed two GOUF Ignited units launched from the Minerva in pursuit from Armory One.\nHowever, those were about its only notable achievements. Afterwards it was cornered by Athrun and others at Junius Seven, defeated by Kira off the coast of Crete, and shot down by Orb's Murasame squadron in Berlin.",
        198: "A mobile suit developed as part of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series.'\nIt is one of three new Gundams stolen from the military plant Armory One by the Earth Alliance special forces unit Phantom Pain. Due to that history, it carries model numbers from both ZAFT (ZGMF-X31S) and the Alliance (RGX-02).\nIt is a highly versatile machine that can be deployed in a variety of combat situations, but it displays its maximum performance especially in underwater combat. When it transforms into its uniquely shaped mobile armor form, it can swim through the water with complete freedom, like a fish in water. It toyed with both Ray's and Lunamaria's ZAKUs simultaneously and also sank the submarine carrier Niragon Goh, among other achievements.\nHowever, it is ironic that its end came when it was pierced by the Blast Impulse Gundam on the water's surface - its own favored field.",
        199: "A mobile suit developed as part of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series.'\nIt is one of three new Gundams stolen from the military plant Armory One by the Earth Alliance special forces unit Phantom Pain. Due to that history, it carries model numbers from both ZAFT (ZGMF-X88S) and the Alliance (RGX-03).\nFollowing in the lineage of the BuCUE and LaGOWE, it can transform into a four-legged beast-type mobile armor form. It specializes in melee combat on land, using its mobility and maneuverability to close in on enemies and slice them in two with its wing-shaped beam blades as its basic tactic.\nIn battle, it fought on par with or better than Lunamaria and Shinn, and also shot down Heine. However, Stella, lacking mental stability, sortied alone on her own authority and was shot down as a result.",
        200: "A mobile suit developed as part of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series.'\nIt is one of three new Gundams stolen from the military plant Armory One by the Earth Alliance special forces unit Phantom Pain.\nThis is the unit that ZAFT recovered after it was rendered inoperable in battle against the Saviour Gundam and Impulse Gundam. During transport to PLANT, the Clyne faction apparently intervened by some means, and it was sent to the Eternal. Afterwards it was repainted in a color scheme reminiscent of the LaGOWE and became Waltfeld's personal machine. However, since Waltfeld needed to serve as captain of the Eternal, it was almost never used.",
        201: "A mobile suit developed by ZAFT as part of the 'Second Stage Series' of new-generation high-performance machines. It was entrusted to Athrun by Durandal when he was appointed to FAITH. The unit is specialized for aerial combat, and by transforming into mobile armor mode it gains even greater mobility and is capable of long-range cruising. It served as the mainstay of the Minerva, which saw much combat over the sea. In battle, it could employ hit-and-run tactics using its high mobility, and confound enemies with attacks that varied in speed. Later, it engaged Kira's Freedom Gundam after a difference of opinion led them into conflict, but found itself at a disadvantage in basic performance against a unit equipped with a Neutron Jammer Canceller, and struggled. Furthermore, Kira's manifestation of SEED proved decisive, and the Saviour was sliced apart by beam sabers.",
        202: "ZAFT's most advanced mobile suit, developed to bring a decisive end to the war with the Earth Alliance. As Shinn grew rapidly, Durandal judged that the Impulse Gundam could no longer fully utilize his talents, and had this unit finely tuned, effectively making it Shinn's personal machine. It is equipped with the 'Hyper Duetrion' power system, which combines a nuclear engine with the Deuterion Beam energy transmission system, and can generate Wings of Light from its wing parts to achieve tremendous mobility. It combines the strengths of all three Impulse Gundam forms, successfully reconciling a versatile arsenal effective at any range with outstanding maneuverability. Furthermore, unique equipment such as palm beam cannons and a afterimage function applying Mirage Colloid was added, realizing the concept of a single unit capable of handling any combat situation. However, the lack of armament on the legs proved to be its undoing; during a melee exchange of kicks with the Infinite Justice, its right leg was destroyed by the Griffon Beam Blade, and it fell to the lunar surface.",
        203: "A state-of-the-art mobile suit developed as an evolution of the Providence Gundam, which was built near the end of the previous war. Initially, it was intended to be given to Athrun, whose performance was highly anticipated, but when Athrun attempted to defect from ZAFT, Ray, who was pursuing him, boarded the unit instead, and it became his favored machine. The 'Dragoon System' mounted on the back has improved response through refinements to the quantum interface, and can be used without being limited by the pilot's spatial awareness. In space, it displays its full potential by deploying all-range attacks with separated units. Within the atmosphere, it can adjust the angle of the units without separating them to deliver multiple attacks in all 360 degrees. It fought on equal terms against Kira's Strike Freedom Gundam, who opposed Durandal. However, Ray was shot down when he was caught off guard by a momentary distraction caused by Kira's words. Notably, at the end of the previous war, a decisive battle was fought between the Freedom Gundam and Providence Gundam, the forerunners of these two units. The fact that the pilot of the Providence Gundam at that time was Rau Le Creuset, a being extremely close to Ray, also speaks to their deep-seated connection.",
        204: "A mobile suit developed by ZAFT near the end of the previous war and entrusted to Kira by Lacus. It was heavily damaged during the final battle of that war against the Providence Gundam, but was secretly repaired in Orb and stored deep within an underground shelter. Although it is an older machine, it is equipped with a Neutron Jammer Canceller, the installation of which is now prohibited on mobile suits. Powered by a nuclear fusion engine, it has no operational time limit and possesses performance capable of overwhelming current-generation units. It was sealed away by Kira, who did not desire conflict, but he was forced to pilot it to protect Lacus and those around him from an assassination squad. Thereafter, it accompanied the Archangel, and was used solely to reduce the mobility and offensive capability of opponents. It was defeated and destroyed beyond recognition by Shinn, who, burning with rage over Stella's death, launched unpredictable multi-layered attacks.",
        205: "A state-of-the-art mobile suit developed alongside the Infinite Justice Gundam at the 'Factory,' a stronghold of the Clyne faction opposing Durandal. It features a gold frame and mounts a new laser nuclear fusion engine, boasting several times the output of the Freedom Gundam. The newly equipped 'Super Dragoon Mobile Weapon System' allows the wing components, which enhance mobility, to separate and be used as wire-guided beam weapons. In its first sortie, it made a brilliant debut by using this new weapon to disable a total of 25 Zaku and GOUF units in just two minutes. Its armor has also been changed to VPS Armor, and it even incorporates a beam shield, making it a machine with no gaps in offense or defense. If there is a single drawback, it is that its performance is so high that no one other than Kira can handle it. Its official designation is 'Strike Freedom Gundam,' but Kira consistently called it 'Freedom.' Unlike the Freedom Gundam, which was heavily damaged at the end of the previous war, this unit finished the conflict in near-perfect condition. It is a main unit more deserving of the title than the one that bears the program's name in its invincibility.",
        206: "The latest mobile suit developed at the 'Factory', the stronghold of the Clyne faction opposing Durandal, alongside the Strike Freedom Gundam. It is a development of the Justice Gundam that Athrun piloted in the previous war, and incorporates technology from ZAFT's 'Second Stage Series'. It is equipped with a laser nuclear fusion engine in its silver frame, and its signature thruster and armament unit, the 'Fatum-01', has been greatly enhanced and improved. The main body is loaded with numerous melee weapons, and in its use as a shock weapon it dealt fatal damage to the Minerva's propulsion system. In the final battle, it was used inside Requiem and succeeded in destroying it. Unlike the Justice Gundam, which left no prototype after being self-destructed in the previous war, this unit finished the fight in almost perfect condition except for the 'Fatum-01'. Perhaps this too is an indicator of Athrun's growth.",
        207: "A mobile suit left to Cagalli by Uzumi Nara Athha, former representative of Orb. Development had progressed since the previous war, but because the latest technology was incorporated each time, it was completed as a high-performance machine rivaling current mobile suits. The Oowashi pack is specialized for use in the atmosphere, and with its equipped flight unit it can fly independently. It carries high-energy beam cannons on both sides, giving it high long-range attack capabilities. Its dazzling gold body is the anti-beam defense and reflection system 'Yatanokagami', which absorbs beams fired at the unit and reflects them after locking onto the enemy. This provides high defensive power and allows the enemy's attacks to be used for counterattacks. However, it cannot fully block physical weapons, so when hit by the Destiny Gundam's Flash Edge 2, its left arm was severed.",
        208: "A mobile suit left to Cagalli by Uzumi Nara Athha, former representative of Orb. When going into space, Neo (Mu), taking over for Cagalli who had to remain in Orb, became its pilot. The Shiranui pack is specialized for space use, and its greatest feature is the 'Guided Mobile Beam Turret System', an improvement on the DRAGOON system that anyone can use. Neo (Mu), who originally had excellent spatial awareness, used it freely, destroying many enemy mobile suits at once on offense and deploying barriers by linking the beam turrets on defense. In the final battle, he thrust his machine between the Archangel's bridge and an incoming barrage. In the same situation during the previous war, the unit was destroyed while stopping the attack, but at this second opportunity, he succeeded in enduring it.",
        209: 'The next-generation mass-produced mobile suit of the Orb military, developed at Morgenroete. It is the successor to the M1 Astray, and its heritage can be seen in the design of its head. As it is intended for carrier operations, it can take a general-purpose mobile suit form and a high-mobility fighter form. Although it is a mass-produced unit, its basic performance is by no means low, and it is a well-balanced machine overall. Through the determination and unity of the Orb military, it performed beyond its specs, cornering the Minerva and shooting down the Chaos Gundam.',
        210: "A Murasame customized for Andrew Waltfeld. Its yellow coloring is distinctive, but the machine's performance is the same as the standard units. It sortied in the Battle of the Dardanelles, and Waltfeld, who claimed to be 'not as skilled as Kira', shot down many Murasames. After Waltfeld returned to the Eternal, Kisaka took his place and sortied in the Orb defense battle.",
        211: "Zamza-Zah was a prototype mobile armor developed by the Earth Alliance. Its crab-like silhouette and enormous size gave those who faced it an overwhelming sense of intimidation. In fact, the Minerva's bridge crew, especially Arthur, were quite shocked upon seeing it for the first time. Despite its massive frame, it possessed unexpected mobility and could attack in all directions with its claws and beam cannons. Furthermore, it could deploy positron reflectors on its front and was a powerful unit capable of repelling even the Minerva's Tannhauser. However, to make full use of its performance, it required three crew members: a commander, a helmsman, and a gunner, in addition to the pilot. The initial type deployed pushed the Impulse Gundam to the brink of being shot down, but that became the trigger for Shinn's SEED to awaken. It was overwhelmed by his dramatically improved movements after the awakening and was ultimately pierced through the cockpit and destroyed.",
        212: "Gells-Ghe was a prototype unit developed by the Earth Alliance that possessed the upper body of a mobile suit, the Strike Dagger, and the lower body of a mobile armor. It boasted high defensive capabilities thanks to its positron reflector, which was primarily deployed for base defense. Unlike the Zamza-Zah's reflector, its positron reflector was deployed toward the front, allowing for rapid switching between offense and defense. It was also well-armed with ranged weapons and displayed unmatched strength in long-range combat. However, on the other hand, it could not adequately respond to close-quarters combat, and after being closed in on by the Saviour Gundam, it was easily shot down.",
        214: "The Destroy Gundam was a massive mobile suit developed by the Earth Alliance and LOGOS at the Adukaf Mechano Industries company. Its stated total length covered only the main unit, and including the rear weapon unit, its size exceeded fifty meters. It maintained a high standard in both offense and defense through the overwhelming firepower of its numerous weapons mounted across its body, thick armor, and the positron reflectors equipped on both arms. In its mobile armor form, where the rear weapon unit covered its upper body, it was also capable of low-altitude flight. It was a unit designed exclusively for Extenders, and Stella piloted the initial production model, engulfing cities across western Eurasia, including Berlin, in flames. The five units produced afterward were deployed in the battle at Heaven's Base, where Sting and the others piloted them and inflicted tremendous damage on the ZAFT fleet. However, all units were destroyed through the combined efforts of Shinn, Ray, and Lunamaria.",
        215: "The Minerva was the latest ZAFT warship built with the goal of operating and coordinating the Second Stage Series units. It was equipped with a catapult compatible with the Silhouette System and the Deuterion Beam transmission system. It could move at high speed regardless of location, whether in space, on the ground, or at sea. Its armaments were also abundant, including positron cannons, beam cannons, solid rounds, gatling cannons, and various missiles for space, ground, anti-aircraft, and torpedo purposes. Moreover, the bridge, which had been a warship's greatest weakness, was shielded during combat, making it an all-purpose battleship that could head into battle without concern. Although it set sail without a proper launching ceremony, it continued to achieve significant results in various locations even before the war began, making its name famous as ZAFT's strongest force. However, during the final battle at Messiah, it was defeated by the Archangel and rendered combat-incapable.",
        216: "The Girty Lue was a special warship operated by Phantom Pain, a special forces unit of the Earth Alliance. Talia referred to it as Bogey One during the pursuit. It was equipped with Mirage Colloid, which was prohibited by treaty, and excelled in stealth operations using it. The ship also contained a maintenance room for Extenders, where psychological adjustments and memory manipulation could be performed at any time. It was used to seize the new Gundams at Armory One and fulfilled that role perfectly. It was also used when Djibril escaped from the Daedalus base on the Moon, but its bridge was crushed by the Legend Gundam's Beam Spike, and the ship was sunk.",
        223: "At Domepolis Urgusk, this Overman was stored by Duke Medaille under the guise of an art object.\nThe Gainer who activated it combined the game champion title 'King' with his own name to call it 'King Gainer'.\nIts weapons include the Chengan, which can be used as both a sword and a gun, the Needler wielded like a dagger, and scatter grenades that release large numbers of bombs. Spare rounds for each are kept in the pouch on its left thigh, allowing tactics such as dual-wielding two Chengan blades.\nWith the Over Skill 'Acceleration', it could move at super speed that created afterimages, but this was only a fraction of its power.\nIn the battle against the fully awakened Overdevil, King Gainer activated its true Over Skills: 'Over Freeze' (the cessation of all motion, the same ability as the Overdevil) and its opposite, 'Over Heat' (the activation of all motion). It drove off the Overdevil with these. Because of this ability, it is speculated that King Gainer may be an Overman created as a servant of the Overdevil, or as one designed to oppose the Overdevil.",
        225: 'A silhouette machine piloted by Gain.\nIt was developed with precision sniping in mind using its 76mm rapid-fire cannon, which is impeccable in both range and power, and it could fire while moving using its mobility, move quickly to terrain suited for sniping, or support its body with both arms to serve as a fixed gun emplacement.\nIts eye-catching large left arm comes from the legendary early Overman Brunhilde. For this reason, it boasts monstrous strength that even surpasses that of an Overman.\nWhen it was attacked by the Desert Netta, Gauli sortied alone in it and was absorbed, resulting in it being caught in the self-destruction and heavily damaged. Even then, the left arm remained unscathed.',
        226: "A patchwork Overman built by combining Gachiko with parts from various other Overmen.\nIts name carries on from the Overman Gain once used as his beloved machine. It is thought to contain the meaning 'Emperor'.\nIts main armaments are a 76mm rapid-fire cannon and Brunhilde's left arm reused from Gachiko. In particular, with the left arm, because its abilities had been analyzed and properly connected, the Over Skill 'Gravity' became usable.\nIn the battle against the Overdevil, it donned Planeta's coat and worked to persuade Gainer. However, before achieving its goal, it was pierced by a spear of ice and fell.",
        231: "An Overman of the Siberian Railway Guard.\nIts Over Skill 'Time Stop' stops the time of anything touched by the stop beam released from its hands. Yassaba used this Over Skill skillfully, such as stopping bullets fired at it, halting weather phenomena like storms or avalanches on snowy mountains to guide enemies, and releasing the stop at an exquisite timing to create openings. By wearing a special stop coat, it could release the stop beam over a wider area.\nIt cornered King Gainer with attacks from four twin launchers on both hands and the ultra-high-heat flamethrower 'Bellows', but a single bullet fired by Gain proved decisive, and it was defeated. After coming into the hands of Yapan's Ceiling, it seems to have been used as repair parts for King Gainer.",
        234: "An Overman owned by the Siberian Railway Guard, also called a Psycho Overman together with the Desert Netta and Lion Netta.\nThe Over Skill 'Telepathy' releases a person's surface consciousness as a voice, so one's thoughts become openly known to those around. Kashmar used this to incite conflict between Yapan's Ceiling and the people of Gangaran.\nIn combat, it also used the ability offensively to read the enemy's thoughts beforehand, displaying combat prowess that even Gain and Gainer together could not penetrate with their attacks. However, when Gainer focused all his nerves on exposing his feelings for Sara, Kashmar lost concentration and stopped the Over Skill. King Gainer exploited that opening and destroyed it.\nWhen Gainer used Over Freeze, Gain draped Planeta's coat over the Emperanza, and it served the role of conveying everyone's inner voices.",
        235: "An Overman used by the Siberian Railway Guard. Its main weapon is only an electric shock ball fired from its beard-like parts, but it possesses the Over Skill 'Phantom', which creates one illusion after another as desired by the pilot. With this, it could appear to divide itself, or project phantoms to confuse enemies. Kejinan used this not only to put on a comedy typical of him, but also to corner King Gainer at one point. However, because the illusions were annihilated at a speed faster than they could be created, the main body was exposed and destroyed.",
        236: "An Overman possessing the Over Skill 'Theft', which could steal any substance, regardless of size, across space. Its original owner was Duke Pilwitz, the lord of Policev, but Asuham took it over in a near-theft manner with extortionate demands, and it can be said that its origin was fitting for such an ability. In battle, it stole a rivet gun from Panther, and even stole bullets and the artificial muscles of the shoulders from King Gainer, but it could not steal Anna's heart and tears. Then Asuham, who was too fixated on Gain, was left open, and the unit was defeated by King Gainer.",
        237: "An Overman given by the Overdevil to Sara, who had been Over Frozen. Sara, gaining the Over Skill 'Theft', which could steal any substance across space, attempted to steal the lives of the leaders of Yapan. However, she was stopped by Adette's Dobeck, had the pouch that was the source of her Over Skill destroyed, and was shot down.",
        238: "An Early Overman of the Siberian Railway Guard. It possessed the Over Skill 'Change', and could become spherical, change parts of its body into swords or shields, and also increase its volume or fire the increased volume outward as projectiles, showing off a transformative versatility that allowed almost anything. Thanks to the extraordinary ability of its pilot, Cynthia, it demonstrated enough performance to annihilate the Asuham Boone special forces unit of St. Reigan with a single unit. After Cynthia withdrew with wounds to her heart, Asuham piloted it, and a second unit that Kids had hidden also appeared.",
        239: "A mass-production type Overman based on the Dominator. Although simplified, it retains transformation capabilities and can also use the Over Skill 'Electric Shock'. Deployed to the Kids Munto guard corps, it fought against the Overdevil and King Gainer, but almost all units were shot down.",
        240: "Overdevil is a mysterious being said to have been sealed by the first Miiya. It possesses its own will and holds the ability to open the ice gate known as the 'Icing Gate.' Though its body parts had been scattered, they were secretly gathered and stored inside a crystal of Agato by Kids, who had learned of its existence. Its Over Skill, 'Over Freeze,' is a terrifying ability that halts not only the movement of matter but also growth, evolution, conscience, and other emotions, and even a black hole - stopping anything, tangible or intangible, without exception. With this power, it manipulated the hearts of Cynthia and Gainer, using them as pawns, and brought the world to the brink of freezing. However, its body was pierced by the Over Heat of King Gainer, piloted by Gainer after he broke free from its control, and it fell to the earth as rain.",
        242: "Big O is a black Megadeus piloted by Roger Smith. It appears from underground when Roger shouts 'Big O, Showtime' into the wristwatch on his left arm, and stands against enemies alongside him. When Roger is aboard, the front monitor displays the spell 'CAST IN THE NAME OF GOD, YE NOT GUILTY.' Normally, it is housed beneath Roger's mansion. But once summoned by Roger, it races through disused underground transit systems via the dedicated transporter 'Prairie Dog' to its destination. It is armed with internal weapons such as the eye-beam 'Arc Line' and the chest and abdomen-launched 'Cannon Party' and 'Missile Party,' but its greatest finishing move is 'Sudden Impact,' a one-hit killing blow that drives the arm's strike pile into the foe. The three units Big O, Big Duo, and Big Fau are beings called 'The Big'; by appearance, Big O is called the Black Big, Big Duo the Red Big, and Big Fau the White Big. In the final phase of the battle with Big Fau, Dorothy, who functioned as Big O's interface, caused each part to deploy and fired a high-output beam from the chest, activating the ultimate move 'Big O Final Stage.' At times, Big O acted on its own as if it possessed a will. When, where, and who manufactured Big O - even Roger, its pilot, did not know.",
        243: 'Mummy is a bandaged Megadeus that appeared at the site of the former John F. Kennedy International Airport. It manipulates the bandages covering its whole body and fires beams from its eyes. It bound Big O with its bandages, but was hit directly by missiles fired by Big O and engulfed in flames. From beneath that blaze, the Red Big - that is, Big Duo - emerged.',
        244: "Big Duo is a flying red Megadeus discovered by Schwarz. If Big O is the Big of the land, Big Duo possesses performance that could be called the Big of the sky. It deploys main wings from both arms, transforms its four fingers into propellers, and flies using the afterburner of its powerful engines. Its armaments include the eye-beam Arc Line, gatling missiles fired from the chest, and megaton missiles stored in both lower legs. It can also rotate its four fingers to grind away the enemy. When it confronted Big O at the Central Dome, it tormented Big O with bombing from the air. However, Roger's quick thinking turned the tables, and it was destroyed. Afterwards, it reacted to Dorothy's presence, advancing on its own without a pilot as if pursuing her, and eventually came to a halt.",
        245: 'Big Duo Inferno is a heavily modified version of the destroyed Big Duo, rebuilt and enhanced by the science division of Paradigm Corporation. It can fly as before the modification, and now wears a face guard during flight. Not only was its design made more menacing, but several performance changes were made, such as hollowed-out gatling missile launch ports. As new weapons, its fingers can transform into knife edges, and the left eye is equipped with an Artemis Arcline. The cockpit uses the interface substitution technology that Beck employed, integrating Alan through countless cables and connectors. As if responding to the will of Schwarz, who had already lost his body, it began acting on its own without accepting Alan as its pilot, absorbed Alan, and vanished into the sky.',
        246: "A white Big Fau piloted by Alex. It was discovered in pieces in a foreign land, so Alex asked the Union to recover it. The parts were loaded onto three Megadeuses and transported to Paradigm City.\nIt was assembled at the Paradigm Corporation's underground factory using the best technology the science division had, but because its core memory was missing, it ran out of control and malfunctioned during its first battle. However, after the memory circuit extracted from Dorothy was installed to serve as the core memory, Alex was able to handle Big Fau completely.\nIts weapons include a tentacle-like beam cannon extending from its back, cannons that emerge from its shoulders, and a corkscrew punch that attacks by spinning the rotors on its arms. By using the rotors as screws, it can move freely through the sea.\nFor a time it overwhelmed Big O, but it lost half its body to the 'Big O Final Stage' and was then destroyed by the suddenly appearing Big Venus.",
        251: "A robot built by Sandman for use against the Zeravire. By uniting the Gran Kaiser as the core with the four Grandivas, God Gravion is completed.\nIt is equipped with an Ergo Form system that forms a graviton field around itself through graviton circulation, multiplying the power of its weapons severalfold. While Ergo Form is active, the weapons and pilot are placed under enormous strain, making prolonged use impossible. When Eiji, burning with rivalry against Tokai, boarded it without permission, he was severely injured by the Ergo Form's backlash. This shows both its power and its danger.\nHowever, since the Gran Kaiser itself is not burdened by gravitons, it has no graviton critical limit.",
        252: "A super robot developed by Sandman for use against the Zeravire.\nIt is completed by the four Grandivas - the G Attacker as the right leg, G Striker as the left leg, G Driller as both arms, and G Shadow as the chest and head - uniting with the core Gran Kaiser.\nThrough the Ergo Form system, the pilot's G Factor is made to resonate with gravitons, multiplying weapon power severalfold. However, the union has a time limit called the graviton critical point. If this is exceeded, the Grandivas will be destroyed, so the union is forcibly cancelled just before reaching criticality - a weakness.\nFor attacks, it uses various weapons built into each Grandiva. From the G Attacker comes the highly homing 'Graviton Missile', from the G Striker the laser whip 'Graviton Viper', the 'Graviton Tornado Punch' which spins and fires the G Driller, the 'Gravity Crescent' which throws the G Shadow's wings, and the 'Graviton Arc' which releases graviton energy from the chest.\nThe 'Choujuuken' (Super Heavy Sword) brought by Sandman in episode 13 is the strongest sword, capable of cutting its target along with the space around it. Besides slashing, it can also be used to seal the enemy's movements with an Ergo Storm before cutting. However, it is originally a weapon for Sol Gravion.",
        253: "A super robot developed by Sandman in preparation for the coming final battle against his brother-in-law Hyugi.\nIt is completed by the four Sol Grandivas - the Geo Caliver as the right leg, Geo Stinger as the left leg, Geo Javelin as both arms, and Geo Mirage as the chest and head - uniting with the core Gran Kaiser.\nThrough the Ergo Form system, it amplifies the pilot's mental energy and explosively releases heavy gravitons. In theory, it possesses the power to not only destroy a star but even create one. Consequently, the Grand Knights who pilot it must be of commensurate ability, so Sandman kept it hidden at a lunar base until they grew into warriors worthy of that power.\nIts main weapons include the 'Sol Graviton Cannon' on both shoulders, the 'Sol Graviton Arc' fired from the chest, the 'Sol Graviton Nova' which concentrates those two, and the 'Sol Graviton Bringer' which charges with the left arm drill spinning. The 'Choujuuken' used by God Gravion is also originally a Sol Gravion weapon.\nBy performing the most sinister union with God Sigma Gravion, it can become the strongest final form, 'Ultimate Gravion'.",
        254: "A super robot completed by the Grandivas uniting with the Souseiki Gran Sigma, a machine capable even of creating stars, which the young Sandman developed to save his homeland of Lambias. Its color scheme is black to match Gran Sigma, unlike God Gravion's blue.\nDespite uniting with Grandivas that operate on the Phantom System, it displayed performance rivaling God Gravion. This feat was only possible through the immeasurable performance hidden within Gran Sigma and, above all, Sandman's own power and skill.\nIts main weapon is the 'Graviton Lancer', formed by combining swords drawn from the waist. With it, Sandman used the 'Sigma Slash', whose blade's trajectory traces a sigma, to easily dispatch the Zeravire that stood in his way.\nIn the final battle against the Zeravire homeworld Goma, it performed the most sinister union with Sol Gravion to become 'Ultimate Gravion', stunning viewers.",
        255: "The Gran Trooper is the main battle machine of the Earth Federation Administration (EFA), and can be called a mass-production version of Gravion. It was developed based on Gravion data sent by Mizuki. Five units were manufactured, and all were assigned to the Gran Trooper squad. The unit piloted by the squad leader, Faye, has red coloring applied in various places.\nIn addition to a humanoid form with high combat capability, it can also transform into a fighter form with high mobility.\nEach Gran Trooper is equipped with different armaments; Faye's unit has two: the 'Gravity Lang', which combines and throws the shoulder parts, and the 'Gravity Arrow', which fires numerous beam shots. Furthermore, by receiving energy supply from each Gran Trooper, it can use the 'Lightning Detonator', which has 1.5 times the destructive power of the Graviton Arc.",
        258: "A Zeravire that appeared in episode 6, 'Touga's Day Off'. Its official name is 'Demon Eye Shikigami Juettal'.\nIt was created to investigate the performance of God Gravion, and its combat capability is lower than other Zeravires. Therefore, it was scattered by Touga and Eiji, who were roused to protect their friends.",
        259: "A Zeravire that appeared in episode 13, 'Silver Fang', created for fighting God Gravion. Its official name is 'Duel War God Hudwell'.\nIt had resistance to all weapons previously used, and drove God Gravion into a corner. However, it was destroyed by a single strike from the Choujuuken, which united the hearts of the Gran Knights.",
        260: "A Zeravire that appeared in episode 3, 'Fierce Battle! Gurabi Hot Springs!!'. Its official name is 'Flame Prison Dragon God Magguard'.\nIt hid within the magma layer and activated volcanic activity, but was defeated by God Gravion, spurred on by the passionate cheering of the maids.",
        261: "A Zeravire that appeared in episode 7, 'The Shattered Goddess'. Its official name is 'Broken Precept Slave God Zalogros'.\nIt exploited a slight opening during Unite, capturing Gran Kaiser. Afterwards, it cornered Touga with a mental attack, but due to Eina's suicide attack, it lost Gran Kaiser, though it heavily damaged the G Driller. Subsequently, it was destroyed by Gran Troopers that appeared suddenly.",
        262: "The mightiest Zeravire to appear from episode 11 'Souseiki', holding within it the energy of the long-extinct planets Lambias and Celia. Its official name is 'Gyomashin Zeravion'. It possessed what seemed to be infinite self-regeneration ability, and even drove Sol Gravion into a corner. However, its programming that prevented it from attacking Leele was exploited in reverse, and the opening created when it halted was seized upon to destroy it with the Choujuuken.",
        263: "A planet that appeared in episode 12 'Anthem of Souls', serving as the home base of the Zeravire. With Hyugi and Zeravion defeated, it transformed itself into a Zeravire and ran wild. It was completely destroyed by the Choujuu Enouzan of Ultimate Gravion.",
        264: "A mechanized angel built by Apollonius 12,000 years ago for use against the Shadow Angels. It is sometimes called the Mythological-Type Aquarion. By combining three Vector Machines, it can transform into three different forms; the order of assembly greatly changes the resulting form and abilities. This is Aquarion's strongest form, completed with Vector Sol forming the upper body, Vector Mars the lower body, and Vector Luna the back. It is characterized by its red-based coloration and sun-motif head, with power stones on both shoulders and both shins that amplify bio-energy and higher-dimensional quantum power. While its armor resists physical attacks and it possesses enormous output, it also demands powerful Element abilities from its pilots, making it almost exclusively Apollo's form. Deploying the solar wings on its back allows it to bring out even greater power. Its main armament is its 'fists' themselves, whose destructive force is so strong that even without using a special technique it can shatter a Cherudim Soldier in one blow. Its special moves are mostly fist-based as well, including the 'Mugen Punch', a desperate punch that reaches the moon, and the 'Kouei Gou Ikkken', delivered in unison by Apollo and Silvia after they realized their true feelings for each other. Incidentally, when Reena is the main pilot, it takes on a silvery gleam and becomes 'Silver Aquarion'. Initially, Apollo, who held the past life of Apollonius, was believed to be the 'Wing of the Sun' who would be the savior. But Zushi, alias Toma, revealed that the true 'Wing of the Sun' was in fact the Aquarion that Apollonius had built with his own wings.",
        270: "A new Aquarion jointly developed by the New United Nations Forces and DEAVA using the wings of Futaba. Called the Assault-Type Aquarion, considerable numbers have been mass-produced. Because Elements who have likewise received transplanted wings pilot it, a single person can control all functions (the other two units are equipped with control units using Shadow Angel wings). This form is completed with Vector Alpha as the head, and carries the massive Impact Cannon that was already eye-catching in Vector Alpha mode. Normally stored in the left arm, when used it loads a Shadow Angel wing and fires the PSG Quantum Cannon, making it a powerful weapon. When Glen, who had fallen into a coma, received the wings of a Celestial Angel and returned to the front lines, he appeared in this machine. In the final battle, Reika piloted it alongside Reena and Pierre, unleashing the last special move 'Fukou Danzetsuken' at the approaching Onshi, and literally parted with her own misfortune. Incidentally, the Assault-Type Aquarion, a form not even present in the original, can transform into an 'Assault Walker form' enabling high-speed ground movement and flight, and a multi-legged artillery 'Armageddon form'.",
        274: "A Cherudim Soldier that appeared in episode 21 'Red Way'. Piloted by the Shadow Angel front-line commander Zushi, alias Toma, its combat ability is among the strongest of the Cherudim Soldiers. It skillfully wielded the swords on both arms, confounding Sirius in his Aquarion Mars. In that battle, Sirius was captivated and defected to the Shadow Angels.",
        275: "In episode 13 'The 10,000 Year Love Letter', this two-seat Cherudim Soldier first appeared piloted by Zushi (Toma) and then by Onshi (Otoha).\nIt possessed agility surpassing that of Aquarion Mars and fought in a dancing style with twin swords fashioned from its waist skirt parts.\nIt completely overwhelmed Aquarion, but was burned to nothing by the 'Fire Flame Thunder Burst' (Kauen Baku Raiha), which Reika created by gathering the abilities of Tsugumi and Pierre into a new form - Aquarion Solna - born from Reika's quick thinking.",
        276: "Appearing from episode 10 'Stars in the Sky, Flowers on the Ground', this was a Cherudim Soldier used exclusively by Ryoshi.\nIts attacks using hammer-like massive fists and its combination fighting when split into two units were intense, and it seriously wounded Silvia. However, it was driven back by the 'Infinite Cross Fist' (Mugen Cross), a special move Apollo and Sirius devised by realizing their own immaturity, crossing their fists with each other.\nIt reappeared later when Apollo and the others forced their way into Atlandia and cornered Glen's Aquarion Omega, but it fell before Glen's attack, which traded away his own life.",
        278: "A Cherudim Soldier appearing in episode 8 'First Combination'.\nIts armor was remarkably hard and deflected every one of Aquarion's attacks. Its drill-like arms could be fired as projectile weapons as well as used for direct blows.\nIt was blasted from within by the joint special move 'Reverse Mental Image Burst' (Gyaku Nenshabakuha), performed by Jun and Tsugumi during their first combination with Aquarion.",
        279: "A Mythical Beast appearing in episode 18 'Soul Cosplayer' that copied Solar Aquarion.\nIts characteristics and attack methods faithfully reproduced those of the original.\nIt was destroyed by the 'Super 3D Infinite Fist' (Ko Jigen Mugen Attack), a special move Apollo, Silvia, and Sirius generated by linking their souls with the different weapons of Aquarion's three forms.",
        280: "A Mythical Beast appearing in episode 18 'Soul Cosplayer' that copied Aquarion Mars.\nIts characteristics and attack methods faithfully reproduced those of the original.\nIt was destroyed by the 'Super 3D Infinite Fist' (Ko Jigen Mugen Attack), a special move Apollo, Silvia, and Sirius generated by linking their souls with the different weapons of Aquarion's three forms.",
        281: "A Mythological Beast that appeared in Episode 18 'Soul Cosplayer', copying Aquarion Luna.\nIts characteristics and attack methods faithfully reproduce the original.\nIt was destroyed by the special move 'Super 3D Infinite Punch', created when Apollo, Silvia, and Sirius linked their souls with the different weapons of the three Aquarion forms.",
        282: "A Mythological Beast that appeared in Episode 5 'King of the Underground Labyrinth'.\nIt has a hand-like shape and can move through the ground.\nIts attack of numerous missiles fired from the back of its hand is powerful, but its position was detected by Aquarion Mars piloted by Pierre, and it was defeated by the special move 'Scorching Fire Gaol'.",
        288: "The most advanced LFO owned by Gekkostate. Its official name is 'Terminus type R909'.\nOriginally, this unit was adopted for regular use by the special mobile forces of the Federation of the Tower State. It achieves outstanding mobility through weight reduction surpassing the R606, and long operating time and high firepower through improved power saving that corrects the R808's flaws. By releasing the limiter, the 'Compact Feedback System' can also be used, making it the highest performance in the series.\nHowever, on the other hand, handling became considerably more difficult, and production costs also rose. Additionally, for the reason that no further improvement in unit performance could be hoped for, it became the unit that brought the Terminus series to an end. Since no one in Gekkostate other than Holland can master it, it has effectively become his personal machine.\nDuring the second encounter with Anemone, he fought the End alone, but was grabbed by its claw and torn apart.",
        293: "A KLF developed by the Federation of the Tower State, modeled after Type Zero. Its official name is 'Nirvash type the END'.\nIn contrast to Type Zero, it has a sinister black body and sharp-angled form. However, it responds to the calls of its rider Anemone, and has eyes on its head, showing many commonalities. It is also distinctive in that it wears two lift boards on both feet like skis.\nIt is equipped with 'Bascud Crisis', which directly attacks the brains of enemy riders, as its primary weapon, as well as wire-guided melee claws and numerous homing lasers. It pursues its target relentlessly, bringing 'the end' to those it faces, as its name suggests. In the battle against the Coralian Antibody, it deployed VC-10s around itself to form 'Formation Gagundura' and unleashed 'Baharuk Swell'.\nIn the end, it evolved just like Type Zero, and gained a pure white body as if responding to Anemone's feelings, but it protected Anemone and Dominic from Dewey's attack and ceased its activity.",
        295: "A large flying-wing battleship operated by the air force of the Federation of the Tower State.\nIt has huge wings that receive Trapar, and moves at high speed along ley lines to transport mounted KLFs and soldiers. It is also equipped with abundant weaponry such as beam cannons, missiles, and depth charges, making its performance as a combat vessel extremely high.\nThe Izumo squad led by Jurgens also uses this ship, so it is also called the 'Izumo ship'. Later, when the Izumo squad left the military to stop Dewey's ambition, it underwent major modifications at the Trezor Institute and was reborn as the 'Super Izumo ship'. At that time, it was painted deep red, the 'hot man's blood'. The red lines on the wings originally indicate Izumo squad affiliation.",
        296: "The Ginga-Goh is the latest cruiser developed by the Federation of the Tower State military. It serves as the flagship of the Ageha Squad, with Dewey aboard as its captain.\nDesigned with the same technological lineage as the Gekko-Goh, it boasts an ultra-large hull approximately 1.5 kilometers in length and 700 meters in width. Despite being such a massive vessel, it carries only a single aircraft: the Nirvash type the END.\nTo mitigate the susceptibility to damage inherent in its enormous size, it is equipped with an automated 'Bit' system that both defends against enemy attacks and launches its own.\nIt proudly demonstrated an ironclad defense, blocking all attacks from the Gekko-Goh, but its stronghold was breached beginning with Holland's suicidal ramming attack.",
        309: 'A crow-type mobile weapon developed by Kaimera.\nIt is designed for collective combat, deployed in large numbers on the front lines to overwhelm the enemy through sheer quantity.\nWhile it possesses the high mobility characteristic of unmanned units, its armor is thin, and it is treated as a nearly disposable weapon.',
        310: 'An upgraded version of the Cornix.\nIts tactics remain based on group combat, but its speed and frame structure have been reinforced, making it adept at hit-and-run tactics.\nThat the enhanced crow-type Cornix was deliberately painted white is a preference of Ji Ederu.',
        311: "A mobile weapon developed by Kaimera.\nIt is the personal unit of Lieutenant Raven General, built to a unique standard separate from the New Federation military's systems.\nIt excels in instantaneous power, mobility, and force, specializes in hit-and-run tactics, and fights with its lion-like mane flying wild, exactly matching Raven's overflowing fighting spirit.",
        313: 'A mobile weapon developed by Kaimera.\nIt is the personal unit of Captain Schran Oper, and its design reflects his intentions, taking on a deliberately provocative and malicious appearance.\nIt focuses primarily on ranged combat from a distance, and combined with its high mobility, it excels at tactics that unilaterally corner the opponent.',
        315: 'A mobile weapon developed by Kaimera. It is the personal machine of Lieutenant Tzine Espio, and its design lines are feminine to suit her. It excels in melee combat with bewitching movements and deceptive power. Additionally, part of its weapon system uses dimensional power, giving it aspects of a test unit for the Chaos Lemures.',
        316: 'A mobile weapon piloted by Tzine Espio. It excels in melee combat with bewitching movements and deceptive power. Tzine dislikes the official designation and uses the nickname Eliphas.',
        318: "A mobile weapon that Edel Bernal had Jiei develop as her personal mount. It gathers the finest technology from various worlds in the multiverse, and together with Edel's superlative piloting ability, it possesses combat power that can change the course of a battle on its own. Edel calls this machine the 'throne of the new world's ruler,' and intends to make it a symbol when she rules the multiverse. For Jieie, it is a prototype for the Chaos Lemures, but it does not mount the system that applies dimensional power.",
        320: 'A jet-black humanoid mobile weapon piloted by Asakim Dowin. It boasts tremendous mobility and toys with enemies through sheer speed. Its main armament is the Demon King Sword Discalibur. It can also transform into a high-speed cruise form. A perpetual engine is built in as its main power source, and it demonstrates various unique abilities, but the technology used and the circumstances of its development are shrouded in mystery.',
    },
}
